diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 013a4e7..8dfe55a 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@ A simple Windows Forms frontend is in `src/SnowPakTool.Desktop`. Its first tab h
 
 All desktop tabs share one double-Shift text search with a three-character minimum. It searches the current tab and selected sub-tab, highlighting labels, values, table text and detail data without filtering rows. Enter focuses the first match; Esc, clicking elsewhere, or switching tabs/windows closes search.
 
-**Editors → Truck properties** lists truck names, classes, assigned tiers, fuel capacity, unlock rank, price, store countries, differential lock and verified obtainable regions/maps. Region information reuses Regions-Trucks, including randomized replacements and pending map changes; unavailable map data and unverified placements are not guessed. Click column headers to sort, or **Order by tier** for SS through FX followed by Unsorted. Hover a truck name to show its usual tile. Edit numeric cells or use the −/+ glyphs to adjust all explicitly defined values (10 L fuel, 1 rank, 1,000 price), bounded to the displayed ranges. Blank/inherited values stay unchanged. **Save preset / Load preset** exports/imports a versioned JSON snapshot; loading only previews matching workspace values. **Stage changes** persists an explicit snapshot across restarts and lists it on Start even before opening this tab. **Revert unstaged edits** restores that snapshot, **Revert staged changes** clears it, and **Reset to original values** previews the preserved baseline. Only Start → Apply pending PAK edits writes the updated workspace files, preserving unrelated XML and the original files; later unstaged edits are excluded. Reload properties discards unstaged edits. Staged values changed externally are rejected during Apply and can be reloaded and restaged.
+**Editors → Truck properties** lists truck names, classes, assigned tiers, fuel capacity, unlock rank, price, store countries, differential lock and verified obtainable regions/maps. Region information reuses Regions-Trucks, including randomized replacements and pending map changes; unavailable map data and unverified placements are not guessed. Click column headers to sort, or **Order by tier** for SS through FX followed by Unsorted. Hover a truck name to show its usual tile. Edit numeric cells individually. The compact fuel multiplier slider selects 0.5× through 3× in 0.5 steps; **Multiply all fuel** multiplies the currently displayed, explicitly defined fuel capacities, rounds to whole litres (halves away from zero), and bounds the results to the allowed range. Moving the slider alone does not change values, and repeated button clicks multiply again. Changed numeric cells show the preserved original in parentheses, e.g. **160 (80)**, with amber preview/staged and green applied highlights; editing and sorting use the numeric value. The **Columns** checkbox dropdown controls visible columns; Differential Lock is hidden and unchecked by default. Blank/inherited values stay unchanged. **Save preset / Load preset** exports/imports a versioned JSON snapshot; loading only previews matching workspace values. **Stage changes** persists an explicit snapshot across restarts and lists it on Start even before opening this tab. **Revert unstaged edits** restores that snapshot, **Revert staged changes** clears it, and **Reset to original values** previews the preserved baseline. Only Start → Apply pending PAK edits writes the updated workspace files, preserving unrelated XML and the original files; later unstaged edits are excluded. Reload properties discards unstaged edits. Staged values changed externally are rejected during Apply and can be reloaded and restaged.
 
 The **Planning** tab contains **Truck tiers** and **Region difficulty**, alongside ownership and truck groups. **Region difficulty** ranks all regions found in the workspace in fixed S, A, B, C, and D tiers, from hardest to easiest: S red, A orange, B yellow, C green, and D blue. The same colors appear on Region progression tiles; truck tier colors are independent. It shares truck tier-list drag-and-drop, reordering, directional scrolling, palette colors, and search, with offline region thumbnails and season labels. Region rankings save automatically in their own file, independently of truck rankings.
 
